WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:06.041
Now we combine the previous two ideas First we clean
each possible

00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:11.416
contact value We trim extra spaces and convert blank
values into null

00:00:12.818 --> 00:00:17.381
Then we use coalesce to choose the first usable
contact method The

00:00:17.407 --> 00:00:21.324
priority in this example is email first then mobile
phone then home

00:00:21.337 --> 00:00:26.981
phone and finally the text No contact provided The
SQL may look

00:00:27.007 --> 00:00:32.735
longer but the logic is actually very systematic Run
the query

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.435
in the browser and look at the preferred contact
column Then try

00:00:37.461 --> 00:00:42.102
copying it into pgAdmin As you read the expression
do not try

00:00:42.128 --> 00:00:47.759
to pronounce every parenthesis Think about the
workflow clean email clean mobile

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:51.496
clean home and then choose the first value that is
actually available
